    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488">

                <pb facs="0454" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/480.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Postmaster
                    General.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-12-06"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence, and
                    especially to the Department’s letter of August 30 last in the case of the
                    newspaper known as the Monitor Democrático,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d488-f1"/> I
                    have the honor to inclose herewith for your information and for such action, if
                    any, as you may consider appropriate, a copy of a letter from Mr. Charles Q.
                    Davis, president of the Bankers Mining &amp; Development Co., Columbus, Ohio, in
                    which he calls attention to articles appearing in the American Magazine entitled
                    “Barbarous Mexico.”</p>
                <p>Mr. Davis states, “We think that the owners and editors of the American Magazine
                    should be prosecuted for libel and the publication denied the use of the
                    mail.”</p>
                <p>For your information I inclose a copy of this Department’s reply to Mr.
                    Davis.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d488-a1.xml" xpointer="d488-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d488-a2.xml" xpointer="d488-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d488-f1" n="1" xml:id="d488-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed (file No. 812.00/38). The Department’s language in the body of the
                    letter to its correspondent (San Antonio Chamber of Commerce) is copied verbatim
                    in Inclosure 2, replying to Mr. Davis.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
